<h1><hr class="Journal2">ROOSTING IN PIGEON FORGE, TN - Monday, November 8, 2004<hr class="Journal2"></h1>
<p>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041108/DSCN0009.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041108/Small/DSCN0009.jpg"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041108/DSCN0001.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041108/Small/DSCN0001.jpg"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041108/DSCN0006.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041108/Small/DSCN0006.jpg"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041108/DSCN0007.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041108/Small/DSCN0007.jpg"></a>
<p>
Today is pretty much a down day for me.  I spend the morning and afternoon chillin' in Pigeon Forge, TN where I while away my time travel writing in the van.  Growing bored, to break up the monotony I entertain myself with the van's heater.  Evening arrives and I get a warning by the cops, I'm told I cannot overnight at the Walmart parking lot.  Rats!  When nightfall arrives, I head due west in search of new overnight digs.  Soon I find a new van camping spot in Rockville, TN where I settle in for the evening and retire for the night.
<p>
