<h1><hr class="Journal2">ROAD TRIP TO HOUSTON, TX - Saturday, November 13, 2004<hr class="Journal2"></h1>
<p>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041113/DSCN0016.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041113/Small/DSCN0016.jpg"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041113/DSCN0146.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041113/Small/DSCN0146.jpg"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041113/DSCN0189.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041113/Small/DSCN0189.jpg"></a>
<a href="index.php?action=Pics&name=Daily/20041113/DSCN0235.jpg&nocomments=1"><img src="Pics/Daily/20041113/Small/DSCN0235.jpg"></a>
<p>
After coming to terms with my fat, gross stomach, I make plans for a full day of driving.  My route today takes me from New Orleans to the heart of Houston.  On the way I encounter a boatload of swampy sights, a number of oil refineries, and the mighty Mississippi River.  I arrive in Houston in the evening and settle into working on the website before retiring late at night.
<p>
